+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Tool definitions declare a JSON Schema for their input, which is handed to AI providers to shape model tool calls. ToolRegistry validates tool call input against the resolved definition's inputSchema before invoking the executor, ensuring unexpected or malformed inputs are caught consistently at the engine boundary.
+
+## Validation Contract
+
+- When a tool call's input does not conform to the registered inputSchema, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a rejection ToolResponse describing the failure without invoking the executor ([validated by: returns a rejection describing missing required input without invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L4)).
+- A validation failure message names the failing property paths and constraint, but never includes the offending property value ([validated by: redacts offending property values from validation failure messages](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L35)).
+- Registering a static tool definition whose inputSchema is uncompilable throws an error naming the tool at registration time ([validated by: throws at registration time for an uncompilable inputSchema naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L72)).
+- Valid input containing unlisted extra properties is passed through to the executor unchanged.
+- Calling `execute` with an unregistered tool name throws an unknown tool error.
+- A dynamic tool definition source is re-evaluated and validated against its current schema on each execution call.
+- A static tool definition's schema is compiled once at registration and reused across execution calls.
